What is UTF-8?
UTF-8 stands for unicode transformation format - 8 bit. It is a character encoding system used to represent text in computers.
For example: The english letter A is represented using 1 byte in UTF-8 while other character requires different number of bytes.

Pros of CSV file
Simple and easy to read
Small size
Easy to import/export
Works with different programming languages and data analysis tools

Cons of CSV file
Cannot store formatting
Cannot store formulas
Cannot contain multiple worksheets in a single workbook
Special character causes issues due to incorrect encoding handling

Pros of XLSX
Supports multiple worksheets
Supports formulas and calculations
Allows formatting, charts, filters etc.
Can preserve different datatypes

Cons of XLSX
Usually requires more space than CSV
Requires spreadsheet-compatible software for accurate use
Complex than CSV


What is Encoding?
It is the process of converting data, specially characters or text, into a specific format that computers can store, process, and transmit.
Different encoding schemes areL UTF-8, UTF-16, ASCII, ISO-8859-1 
